Subject: Tweak: Feder's fair ball contests
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

cGame::Update updates the ten players one at a time in the order of
m_pRandomPlayersArray, and when two of them can take the ball in the same
step, the one updated first takes it (cPlayer::CanPickupBall sees the ball
still loose). RandomizePlayerUpdateOrder sets that order at every kickoff
(ResetCharacters): the home team's five players, then the away team's,
then each slot swapped with any of the ten. Of those 10^10 equally likely
swap sequences some orders come out more often than others: a home player
is updated before a given away player in 52.3 % of kickoffs on average and
in up to 55.4 % for some pairs, and the order holds until the next kickoff.

Some contests are settled after the physics step instead. PostPhysicsAITask
calls PrePhysicsUpdate on the characters in g_pCharacters order: the home
fielders (slots 0-3), the away fielders (4-7), then the two goalies. There
cFielder::TestAnimBallContact gives the ball to the first fielder whose
one-timer, first-time shot or pass off a loose ball, or pass reception
touches it while it is still loose, so when fielders of both teams touched
it in the same step, the home fielder always took it.

With "Feder's fair ball contests" enabled, contests go to the defending
team, the one whose goal is on the ball's side of the field (the ball's x
times its net's m_fDirection is positive). Every step shuffles the order
again and then moves the defending team's five players ahead of the other
five, each team keeping its shuffled order, so no player of a team is ahead
of a teammate for a whole kickoff. At kickoff the ball is on the center line
(x = 0) and the order stays shuffled only. The shuffles are Fisher-Yates
(slot i takes one of the slots from i on), where every order is equally
likely; the kickoff one draws as many numbers as the original, so the
match's random sequence (gNetworkRandomSeed) is unchanged. The per-step
shuffles draw from their own seed, set at each kickoff from the match's seed
without advancing it, and leave every other random event of the match as in
the original. PostPhysicsAITask then follows the step's update order too
(cGame::FairBallContestsOrder); nothing else it does depends on the order,
as each fielder only updates itself and the opposing goalie's deke on it.
Named after Feder, who made a Gecko code for this on the Wii release.
Online matches always play with the tweak, whatever the
setting: both machines must update the players in the same order, and the
order is part of the state they checksum (cGame::SyncLog), so a machine
without it falls out of sync at the first check after kickoff.

